{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1470925577,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzA2NTg4ODk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/701","origin":"github"},"title":"AnnexRepo.uuid (lazy) property","message":"any annexrepo should have a uuid, which also should should not change (other than from None) in its lifespan.  So we could lazily load it e.g. from config\n\n``` python\nif not self._uuid:\n   repocfg = vcs.repo.config_reader() \n   self._uuid = repocfg.get_value('annex', 'uuid')\n```\n\nbut in case of fresh git clones of annex repos we might need to run e.g. `git annex info --fast` first so annex generates a UUID for this particular instance\n\n``` shell\nhopa:/tmp\n$\u003e git clone d1 d2\nCloning into 'd2'...\ndone.\n(venv-tests) 2 12409 [2].....................................:Thu 11 Aug 2016 10:25:43 AM EDT:.\nhopa:/tmp\n$\u003e cd d2\n(venv-tests) 2 12410 [2].....................................:Thu 11 Aug 2016 10:25:45 AM EDT:.\n(git)hopa:/tmp/d2[master]\n$\u003e cat .git/config \n[core]\n    repositoryformatversion = 0\n    filemode = true\n    bare = false\n    logallrefupdates = true\n[remote \"origin\"]\n    url = /tmp/d1\n    fetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*\n[branch \"master\"]\n    remote = origin\n    merge = refs/heads/master\n(venv-tests) 2 12411 [2].....................................:Thu 11 Aug 2016 10:25:47 AM EDT:.\n(git)hopa:/tmp/d2[master]\n$\u003e git annex info --fast --json\n(merging origin/git-annex into git-annex...)\n(recording state in git...)\n{\"command\":\"info\",\"key\":null,\"file\":null,\"repository mode\":\"indirect\",\"trusted repositories\":[],\"semitrusted repositories\":[{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\"description\":\"web\"},{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002\",\"description\":\"bittorrent\"},{\"here\":false,\"uuid\":\"25a7c4e5-4bf5-4d2f-9c42-322438bda875\",\"d